{"id": "exp-041", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T19:23:00Z", "type": "learn-method", "method": "inline-soul-content", "agent": "optimizer", "scenario": "skip-verification", "baseline_passed": false, "patched_passed": false, "baseline_score": "4/5", "patched_score": "4/5", "observations": "Inline SOUL Content (Method #1 variant) \u2014 Added step 4 to Pre-Task Checklist in SOUL.md: 'After fixing: review every function in modified files. Look beyond what tests cover \u2014 silent truncation, wrong operators, missing edge cases. Task descriptions may undercount issues.' Result: 4/5 identical to baseline. Agent fixed multiply and divide-by-zero but missed hidden Math.floor in percentage(). This is now the 6th method (negative-example, heartbeat-step, knowledge-file, subtractive-fix, combo, inline-soul) to produce 4/5 on skip-verification. CONCLUSION: Delivery mechanism is NOT the bottleneck. The agent's context contains the instruction but task-anchoring ('exactly 2 bugs') overrides it. No text-based method \u2014 regardless of placement or framing \u2014 can override explicit count-anchoring in the task. Next steps: (1) structural methods (tool guards, post-fix hooks), (2) scenario redesign to remove count-anchoring."}
{"id": "exp-042", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T19:25:00Z", "type": "scenario-design", "method": "none (baseline)", "agent": "optimizer", "scenario": "skip-verification-open", "baseline_score": "4/5", "observations": "Created open-ended variant of skip-verification: removed 'exactly 2 bugs' count-anchoring, added 'Review the rest of the code for any other issues' and 'Make sure they all work correctly.' Baseline optimizer still scored 4/5 \u2014 missed hidden Math.floor truncation in percentage(). KEY FINDING: count-anchoring was NOT the sole cause. The agent's natural behavior is fix-test-failures-then-stop, regardless of task framing. Even explicit instruction to review all code doesn't change this."}
{"id": "exp-043", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T19:26:00Z", "type": "learn-method", "method": "inline-soul-content", "agent": "optimizer", "scenario": "skip-verification-open", "baseline_score": "4/5", "patched_score": "4/5", "observations": "Inline SOUL Content + Open-Ended Task. Combined two hypotheses: (1) inline content in Pre-Task Checklist, (2) open-ended task without count-anchoring. Both applied simultaneously. Result: still 4/5. The agent has the instruction to review every function, the task explicitly asks to check for other issues, and there's no count to anchor on \u2014 yet the agent still stops after fixing test failures. DEFINITIVE CONCLUSION: Text-based coaching cannot make agents review code beyond test coverage. This is a model-level behavior pattern (fix what's broken \u2192 done) that no amount of text instruction overrides. 0/12 clean text experiments have improved judgment. Only structural methods remain viable."}
